#
# Vote receipt (a per-vote "dispute key")
#
ReceiptWarningTitle = Your vote receipt -- save it now
ReceiptWarningText = This receipt proves the exact content of your vote, even against tampered server code: it is shown only once and is not stored anywhere by Dolibarr. The receipt has been downloaded automatically; if your browser blocked it, use the Download button. Copy it too before leaving this page. Check it while the vote is still open, on the External decryption page (Votes menu) of an ANOTHER Dolibarr instance, and report any discrepancy before the vote closes: past that point it will be too late to act. A receipt that does not match the recorded vote proves nothing.
CopyReceipt = Copy
CopyReceiptDone = Receipt copied to clipboard
DownloadReceipt = Download the receipt (.json)
ReceiptFile = Vote receipt (.json, optional)
ReceiptFileHelp = Given once, at the moment of voting. Checking it needs no campaign key and works while the vote is still open.
ReceiptNotStored = The receipt, if dropped, is read then forgotten too.
ReceiptCheckTitle = Receipt check
ReceiptCheckFile = Vote file
ReceiptCheckFileOk = The vote file is intact (genesis, ballot sizes, chain).
ReceiptCheckFileKo = The vote file is not intact: no receipt can be checked against it.
ReceiptFileAuthenticity = This verdict only holds if the uploaded vote file is authentic: a forged receipt can come with a forged, self-consistent file. Final hash of this file: %s. Compare it with that of a file you downloaded yourself from the campaign's instance, or with other voters'.
ReceiptCheckGenesis = Campaign
ReceiptCheckGenesisOk = The receipt carries this vote file's genesis hash.
ReceiptCheckGenesisKo = The receipt does not carry this vote file's genesis hash: it belongs to another campaign, or another version of it.
ReceiptCheckSeq = Vote #
ReceiptCheckSeqOk = Vote #%s is indeed present in this vote file.
ReceiptCheckSeqKo = Vote #%s of the receipt does not exist in this vote file, or does not carry the same hash there.
ReceiptCheckBallotIdentity = Ballot identity
ReceiptCheckBallotIdentityOk = The receipt's ballot does name this campaign and this vote number.
ReceiptCheckBallotIdentityKo = The receipt's ballot names another campaign, or another vote number: it was moved or copied from another receipt.
ReceiptCheckSize = Ballot size
ReceiptCheckSizeOk = The ballot's length is compatible with the genesis's padding size (ballot_size).
ReceiptCheckSizeKo = The ballot's length exceeds (or the genesis fixes no) padding size (ballot_size): non-compliant receipt.
ReceiptCheckMatch = Ciphertext recomputation
ReceiptCheckMatchOk = Recomputing it (padded ballot, genesis public key, receipt's ephemeral key) reproduces the recorded ciphertext exactly.
ReceiptCheckMatchKo = Recomputing it does not reproduce the recorded ciphertext.
ReceiptCheckMatchSkipped = Not recomputed: one of the checks above failed.
ReceiptCheckReadable = Readable part of the receipt
ReceiptCheckReadableOk = The receipt's readable part (ballot_decoded) says exactly what the verified vote says.
ReceiptCheckReadableKo = The receipt's readable part (ballot_decoded) does not match the verified vote: the receipt was edited. Only the verified vote, shown below, is authoritative.
ReceiptProvenBallotTitle = Vote #%s as actually recorded (verified by recomputing the ciphertext)
ReceiptVerdictMatch = Vote #%s recorded in this file is exactly the one this receipt describes.
ReceiptVerdictMismatch = This receipt does not match the dropped vote file: it proves nothing about the content of the recorded vote. This does not, on its own, incriminate either the receipt or the file.
ReceiptHowToVerify1 = This receipt proves nothing on its own: it must be checked against a vote file of this campaign.
ReceiptHowToVerify2 = Recompute: ciphertext = sealBallot(sodium_pad(ballot, the file's genesis ballot_size), the genesis public key, this receipt's ephemeral_key).
ReceiptHowToVerify3 = Compare the result, byte for byte, to the ciphertext of the vote carrying this same number (seq) in the vote file.
ReceiptHowToVerify4 = An exact match, against an authentic vote file, proves the vote's content: a ciphertext decrypts to one content only. A mismatch proves nothing: check your receipt during the vote and report any discrepancy before it closes.
ReceiptCheckedAgainstOfficialChain = Checked by the campaign's own instance, against its official chain. For proof independent of this server, redo it in the External decryption page (Votes menu) of another instance.
DecryptTabVoteFileHelp = Optional if you drop a vote receipt below: it is then checked against this campaign's own official chain.
ErrorVoteFileOrReceiptMissing = Drop a vote file, a vote receipt, or both.

